* ifndef with a macro's name as a guard (ifndef Flag: r68 knows macros there, gas only symbols;
* the second definition redefined the macro); a parameter that is empty when the body expands
* (Flag \2, called with an empty \2) counts no argument in the inner call; an argument named
* like subi (SUBI) is a mnemonic only where the body uses it as an operation.
* fixed: 0257e62 2026-10-11 r68togas: ifdef of a macro; \# in nested calls; mnemonic arguments; \'
* expect text: 03000001
Flag MACRO
 ifne \#
m\1 equ 1
 endc
 ENDM
 ifndef Flag
Flag MACRO
 dc.b 99
 ENDM
 endc
R2 MACRO
 Flag \2
 Flag \3
 dc.b \#
 ENDM
 psect macro_guard,0,0,0,0,0
 R2 x,,SUBI
 dc.w mSUBI
 ends
